<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yashwant Rao Holkar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1776–1811</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Yashwantrao Holkar I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yashwant Rao Holkar was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> ruler of Indore from 1799 to 1811. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scindias">Scindias</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Poona</a> in 1802, and in 1804–1805 fought the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, routing Colonel Monson's column in 1804 before making peace at Rajghat in 1805.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yashwant-rao-holkar.jpg" alt="Yashwant Rao Holkar" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yashwant_Rao_Holkar_of_Indore.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
